## Migrations

Run this once before starting the app for the first time — it generates
the initial migration from the models in `src/{{ package_name }}/models.py`
and applies it, creating the schema:
{% if orm == "flask-sqlalchemy" %}

```
uv run flask --app src/{{ package_name }}/main.py db migrate -m "describe your change"
uv run flask --app src/{{ package_name }}/main.py db upgrade
```
{% else %}

```
uv run alembic revision --autogenerate -m "describe your change"
uv run alembic upgrade head
```
{% endif %}

Repeat both commands (with a new message) whenever you change a model.
Review every autogenerated migration before applying it.
{% endif %}
{% if worker != "none" %}

## Background worker

```
PYTHONPATH=src uv run celery -A {{ package_name }}.worker.celery_app worker --loglevel=info
```

`PYTHONPATH=src` is needed because the app lives under `src/` — without
it the worker can't find `{{ package_name }}`.
{% if broker == "redis" %}
Needs Redis running and reachable at `REDIS_URL` (see `.env`).
{% elif broker == "rabbitmq" %}
Needs RabbitMQ running and reachable at `RABBITMQ_URL` (see `.env`).
{% endif %}

Try it: `POST /tasks/add?a=1&b=2` enqueues a task and returns its id —
independent of the Todo list, a starting point for your own background
jobs.
{% endif %}
{% if redis %}

